  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nReturn flow around high pressure south of New England will allow\na warming trend to continue into Monday when highs south of the\nmountains push into the upper 60s to low 70s. A weak cold front\ncrosses during the afternoon bringing some clouds and some\nshowers near the Canadian Border. A new Canadian high pressure\nsystem builds in behind the front with highs on Tuesday in the\n40s and 50s followed by overnight lows in the 20s.\n\nThe high starts to shift offshore Wednesday and Thursday\nallowing temperatures to moderate again. Another weak front\ncrosses late Thursday into Friday bringing low chances for\nshowers. High pressure returns behind the front providing mostly\ndry weather to close out the week.",
